#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:2
msgid "Display channel banners"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-adv.rst:7
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry and Enterprise Advanced "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ plans"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:7
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.9, users with admin permissions can enable channel "
"banners to remind channel members about being diligent to avoid data "
"spillage in channels that aren't intended for classified or sensitive "
"information. These non-dismissible banners can be styled using Markdown "
"and are visible across all Mattermost clients, including web browsers, "
"the desktop app, and the mobile app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:9
msgid "Channel banner use cases include the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:11
msgid ""
"Security classifications, such as **SENSITIVE INFORMATION: IMPACT LEVEL "
"5** with a distinctive color to alert members of the required security "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:12
msgid ""
"Important notices, such as **Reminder: Code complete deadlines are "
"Fridays at 3 PM**, for recurring reminders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:13
msgid ""
"Policy or terms, such as  **All discussion in this channel is private and"
" restricted** with a red color to signal caution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:15
msgid ""
"Mattermost :ref:`channel admins <end-user-guide/collaborate/learn-about-"
"roles:channel admin>`, :ref:`team admins <end-user-guide/collaborate"
"/learn-about-roles:team admin>`, and :ref:`system admins <end-user-"
"guide/collaborate/learn-about-roles:system admin>` can enable a banner "
"with custom text at the top of Mattermost public or private channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:17
msgid "Create a channel banner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:19
msgid "Open a channel where you have administrative permissions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:20
msgid ""
"Select the channel name at the top of the center pane to access the drop-"
"down menu, then select **Channel Settings**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:21
msgid "Select **Configuration** and enable the **Channel Banner** option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:22
msgid ""
"Specify the banner text you want to display at the top of the channel. "
"You can style the text using :ref:`Markdown <end-user-guide/collaborate"
"/format-messages:use markdown>`, if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:23
msgid "Select the banner color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:24
msgid "Select **Save** to apply the changes. The banner displays immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:27
msgid "Change a channel banner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:29
msgid ""
"You can change the banner text or color at any time by following the same"
" steps above. The new banner text or color displays immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:32
msgid "Remove a channel banner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:34
msgid ""
"Disable the **Channel Banner** option in the channel settings to remove "
"the banner from the channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/display-channel-banners.rst:38
msgid ""
"System admins can grant any user the ability to create and manage channel"
" banners by assigning the **Manage Channel Banners** permission in the "
"System Console. See the :doc:`advanced permissions </administration-"
"guide/onboard/advanced-permissions>` documentation for details."
msgstr ""

